            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Patricia Tripenfeldas"
            },
            "reviewBody": "this is a authentic Navajo recipe, except its not warm milk exactly you add just a touch of milk to water and heat it warm to the touch, and you should knead it about 15 to 20 times and let the dough rise for at least 4 hrs. that is how you get nice big bread because it'll stretch like you want it to . that is how my mother and auntie did it my whole life. they are from tuba city, Arizona on the Navajo reservation.",
            "datePublished": "2018-10-10T19:38:31.557Z"
          },
