            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This one called pisi in Turkey where they are made with fresh yeast or baking powder. They are baked solo, stuffed with feta cheese or spiced cooked potatoslices or meat. I prefer the ones with yeast and an egg additional to keep them away from soaking much frying oil. The preference is all about the pillowness and staying longer fresh. Can also be deepfreezed--&gt; take out and microwave them slowly. They will be almost like fresh baked.",
            "datePublished": "2023-05-19T20:42:13.471Z"
          },
