            },
            "reviewBody": "Hi, I am a Cree woman and I have been making fry bread all my life. As I was adding the flour, bp and salt and warming the milk up, I was thinking too much liquid and I should have stopped myself. 4 cups of flour and 2 1/2 cups of milk i thought this wont come together but because this is what your recipe calls for, so i followed it. LOL 2 cups of flour later it finally started to be mouldable. I wonder if it has to do with the sea level. When i combined wet and dry i had more of a pancake batter. But in the end they tasted really good. Why using same recipe would there be such drastic results. Why?",
